    "goal": "Size the binary .bed storage footprint for a GWAS genotype dataset of 13971 samples and 7085841 variants, including per-chromosome files.",
    "rationale": "The binary PLINK .bed format packs 2 bits per sample per variant (4 samples/byte). Whole-dataset size = n_samples × n_variants / 4 / 1e6 MB. Per-chromosome size uses the same rule applied to the largest chromosome's variant count (1343865). Number of per-chromosome files equals the number of chromosomes in the dataset; for a standard human GWAS this is 25 (22 autosomes + X + Y + MT).",
